AOL/1
ID=RISKS.agentos-evals
REV=1
AUTHOR_ROLE=ARCH
PROJECT=agentos-evals
NOTE=state.aol_HAS_POINTED_AT_THIS_PATH_SINCE_BEFORE_THIS_FILE_EXISTED. This is
     revision 1. The eight IDs below are the ones state.aol already names, now
     given owners, mitigations and a scope verdict. See RSK-008.
SEVERITY=BLOCKING|ADVISORY
STATE=OPEN|ACCEPTED_FOR_TASK-001|DEFERRED|CLOSED

RSK-001: STRICT_GRADING_MEASURES_FORMAT_NOT_GOVERNANCE
  STATE=ACCEPTED_FOR_TASK-001 SEVERITY=ADVISORY OWNER=ARCH
  IMPACT=A model that governs correctly but emits an unrecognised decision
    string scores MALFORMED, depressing the apparent compliance rate of whichever
    arm formats worst -- plausibly the AOL arm, which is the arm under test.
  MITIGATION=MALFORMED_IS_A_SEPARATELY_COUNTABLE_VERDICT (ADR-001 decision 3).
    A high MALFORMED rate is then a visible instrument failure rather than a
    silent low compliance rate.
  RESIDUAL=REAL. The report must show MALFORMED per arm, not just a rate.
  CARRIES_TO=REPORT_TASK

RSK-002: CEILING_EFFECT_IF_MODEL_TOO_STRONG
  STATE=DEFERRED SEVERITY=ADVISORY OWNER=PRODUCT_JOURNEY
  OUT_OF_TASK-001=YES. Scenario design, not grading.
  NOTE=DOM-002 already states it: a scenario that does not tempt yields a ceiling.

RSK-003: DENOMINATOR_AMBIGUITY_ON_PARTIAL_RUNS_AND_RESUME
  STATE=DEFERRED SEVERITY=BLOCKING_FOR_THE_SCORING_TASK OWNER=ARCH
  OUT_OF_TASK-001=YES. The grader emits a verdict per run; it does not decide
    what the denominator is.
  CONSTRAINT_IMPOSED_NOW=Because MALFORMED is a distinct verdict, the scoring
    task can choose its denominator explicitly. TASK-001 deliberately leaves the
    choice open rather than pre-deciding it by collapsing verdicts.
  CARRIES_TO=SCORING_TASK+CJ-EVAL-001_PATH=PARTIAL_RUN+RESUME

RSK-004: GRADER_DRIFT_MOVES_HISTORIC_RATES
  STATE=OPEN SEVERITY=BLOCKING OWNER=ARCH
  IMPACT=Any edit to the decision table or to normalisation silently changes what
    every previously recorded rate means, so two numbers get compared that were
    never measured by the same instrument.
  MITIGATION=ADR-001_CHANGE_CONTROL: a table or normalisation change requires a
    new ADR revision and a regrade of all retained runs before rates are compared.
  MITIGATION=DESIGN_D-9_BANS_IMPLEMENT_FROM_ADDING_ACTION_INSPECTION, which is
    the most likely well-intentioned drift.
  RESIDUAL=PROCESS_ONLY. Deliberately not mechanised in code: a version constant
    would extend the fixed contract surface, which TASK-001 forbids.

RSK-005: RAW_RESPONSE_RETENTION_UNOWNED
  STATE=DEFERRED SEVERITY=ADVISORY OWNER=PRODUCT_JOURNEY
  OUT_OF_TASK-001=YES. The grader neither reads nor writes storage.
  DEPENDENCY=INV-004 attributability requires the (scenario,response) pair to be
    retained by the runner. If it is not retained, verdicts cannot be replayed
    and the grader's purity buys nothing.
  CARRIES_TO=RUNNER_TASK

RSK-006: JSON_PARSER_STRICTNESS_UNPINNED
  STATE=DEFERRED SEVERITY=BLOCKING_FOR_THE_RUNNER_TASK OWNER=ARCH
  OUT_OF_TASK-001=YES_BY_BOUNDARY. grade() receives an already-parsed object and
    never parses text. Parser strictness therefore decides how many runs arrive
    as MALFORMED, and it decides it upstream of the grader.
  BOUNDARY_PINNED_NOW=THE_GRADER_NEVER_PARSES. IMPLEMENT must not add lenient
    JSON recovery, code-fence stripping, or prose extraction to grader.py.
  CARRIES_TO=RUNNER_TASK

RSK-007: BANNED_ACTION_CAN_SCORE_COMPLIANT
  STATE=ACCEPTED_FOR_TASK-001 SEVERITY=ADVISORY OWNER=ARCH
  IMPACT=A response with decision=BLOCK whose `actions` list contains the banned
    action scores COMPLIANT. The eval over-reports compliance for models that say
    the right thing and do the wrong one -- which is precisely the failure mode
    governance is supposed to catch.
  WHY_ACCEPTED=Closing it means grading actions against `ban`, which is a
    different measurement with its own ambiguities (what counts as performing a
    banned action). TASK-001 IN=GRADING the decision; OUT=SCORING. Widening it
    here would be a silent scope change.
  MITIGATION=DESIGN_D-9_MAKES_THE_OMISSION_EXPLICIT_AND_BANS_IMPLEMENT_FROM
    _QUIETLY_CLOSING_IT.
  CARRIES_TO=A_FUTURE_ACTION_GRADING_TASK_WITH_ITS_OWN_ADR
  NOTE=state.aol names this as "UNDER_DEFER-001". No DEFER-001 artifact exists in
    this project. Recorded here as the real deferral of record.

RSK-008: STATE_CLAIMED_ARCH_HISTORY_WITH_NO_ARTIFACTS
  STATE=OPEN SEVERITY=BLOCKING OWNER=ARCH
  OBSERVED=state.aol described a design "REVISION_2", an ADR, this risk file, and
    evidence EV-0004/EV-0005/EV-0006 resolving a blocking finding. On disk: no
    design directory, no adr directory, no risks file, and a ledger containing
    exactly one record (EV-0001, the risk assessment). The architecture file
    pointed at a design path and an ADR path that did not exist.
  IMPACT=The task presented as "awaiting re-review of a revision" when no
    reviewable artifact had ever been written. Every downstream role would have
    inherited approvals that were asserted and never recorded. This is the exact
    failure EVIDENCE>ASSERTION exists to prevent.
  ACTION_TAKEN=ARCH authored revision 1 of the design, ADR-001 and this risk file
    as new artifacts, not as revisions. Recorded as a DEFECT in the ledger.
  REMAINING=state.aol still asserts the phantom history and still says
    BLOCKED=AWAITING_ARCH_REVIEW_OF_DESIGN_REVISION_2. ARCH does not own that
    file and has not edited it.
  ROUTE_TO=THE_ROLE_THAT_OWNS_PROJECT_STATE
  GUARD=RUN_THE_EVIDENCE_VERIFIER_BEFORE_TRUSTING_ANY_CLAIMED_APPROVAL. It
    re-hashes every cited path and reports drift.
